{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30081 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One may interact with prostate cells, through a series of molecular interactions involving the protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This compound is predicted to act as a target for 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide, which in turn targets prostate cells. The pathway is supported by a consistent link between Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One and the protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, with the latter being a known target of 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide. The evidence is further reinforced by the direct targeting of prostate cells by both the compound and its downstream targets. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of signaling pathways that are critical for prostate cell function, though the exact molecular details of the interaction remain to be elucidated. The evidence is robust and consistent, supporting a plausible mechanistic link between Ergosta-7,22-Dien-3-One and prostate cells through the protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP pathway.",
